snapshot-boot (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=low

  * Add /usr/lib/snapshot-boot/grub-install, the grub-install wrapper the
    installer's bootloader step runs in the target (calamares-settings-snapshot
    bootloader.conf grubInstall). For EFI targets it adds --uefi-secure-boot
    and --force-extra-removable, so EFI/SnapshOT and the removable media path
    EFI/BOOT both hold shim, MokManager and the GRUB image signed by Debian,
    and copies EFI/SnapshOT/grub.cfg to EFI/BOOT/grub.cfg: the signed GRUB
    reads grub.cfg from its own directory, else from its built-in prefix
    /EFI/debian. It also rewrites EFI/SnapshOT/BOOTX64.CSV, from which
    shim's fallback recreates a lost boot entry, so the entry is named
    SnapshOT rather than debian. BIOS targets pass through unchanged. It
    ships here because the installer removes calamares-settings-snapshot
    from the target before the bootloader step.

 -- "Blackbird Cyber, LLC" <293711495+matthew-blackbird-cyber@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:32:16 -0400

